    fix(scaffold): write a build.yaml with a generate stage in `speclang new` (DF-SPECLANG-020)
    
    A freshly scaffolded project shipped no build.yaml, so the daemon loaded its
    defaults (on_converge: []) and the first save converged and then failed the
    pipeline with zero generated files:
    
      [Pipeline] No config file found at build.yaml, using defaults
      [PipelineExecutor] No pipeline stages configured ... nothing to run.
      [Daemon] Pipeline failed (consecutive failure 1): ...
      [Daemon] Cascade NOT complete - pipeline did not succeed.
    
    `speclang new` now writes the smallest pipeline that does what the scaffold
    README already promised - generate code from the specs after a converge:
    
      pipeline:
        on_converge:
          - name: generate
            run: "node scripts/speclang.cjs generate"
    
    The stage goes through scripts/speclang.cjs, so it needs no install and no
    `speclang` on PATH (and no bun). No on_success actions: a scaffold must never
    commit on the user's behalf. convergence/recovery are omitted on purpose -
    src/pipeline/config.ts defaults already cover both. The scaffold README's file
    layout now lists build.yaml and says what the pipeline does with it.
    
    Verified in scratch projects with the shipped CLI:
    - AC1 scaffold contains build.yaml; loaded through PipelineConfigManager it
      validates ({valid:true, errors:[]}) and yields exactly one stage,
      generate = "node scripts/speclang.cjs generate".
    - AC2/AC3 daemon started, a second @block::second @kind:code section appended:
      src/generated/main.spec-second.ts appeared ~30s later (quietPeriod), log shows
      "Loaded config from build.yaml" + "Pipeline succeeded!", and grep counts are
      Pipeline failed = 0, Cascade NOT complete = 0.
    - AC4 `speclang validate` still exits 0.
    - AC5 a second `speclang new` took 0.11s and still wrote specs/main.spec.md.
    - npm test: 2073 passed | 58 skipped (2071 baseline + the 2 new scaffold tests).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
